://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 1:49PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest and west central Colorado, including\nthe following areas, in southwest Colorado, Northwest San Juan\nMountains and Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River. In west central\nColorado, Uncompahgre Plateau and Dallas Divide.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is likely with additional rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms expected through Thursday night. The potential for\nflooding impacts continues into Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:18PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by thunderstorms and excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Western Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern Hinsdale County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT Tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1212 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in\nthe warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain have fallen over\nthe last 24 hours.\n- This includes but is not limited to the following streams...\nVallecito Creek, La Plata River, Animas River and many creeks and\ntributaries that feed into these rivers.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, La Plata, Falfa, Hesperus, Bondad, Breen, Mayday, Kline,\nMarvel, Redmesa and Vallecito.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.98214017c22b766bd2c736aa82684dc784400df5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.98214017c22b766bd2c736aa82684dc784400df5.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-22T19:15:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221915 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 115 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rain continues through early Friday. - Flooding/Flash Flooding is likely across portions of southwest Colorado and southeast Utah. - Modeled responses suggest several rivers reaching bankfull or higher at river forecast points across southwest C","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","iss